Package: attest
Title: Check Whether RNA-Seq Count Data Can Support the Analysis Run on It
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Amir", "Shahbazi", email = "shahbazigenomics@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Audits an RNA-seq count matrix, its sample sheet and its design
    before differential expression analysis with tools such as 'DESeq2',
    'edgeR' or 'limma'. It does not analyse expression. Each check
    adjudicates one claim - that the values are raw counts rather than CPM,
    TPM or normalised values; that every row is a gene named once; that the
    matrix has not been filtered upstream; that samples match their labels;
    that the design can estimate the effect of interest and that no sample
    sheet column left out of the formula lines up with it - and returns a
    verdict, the evidence behind it, and the checks the inputs could not
    answer. A separate scope report states, per gene, the smallest fold
    change the data could have detected.
URL: https://github.com/shahbazigenomics/attest
BugReports: https://github.com/shahbazigenomics/attest/issues
